WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.867
Value function.

2
00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.679
How good is it to be here?

3
00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:07.633
An agent that can answer that never has to simulate what comes next.

4
00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:12.600
A value function answers: how good is it to be here, as a number.

5
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.833
V of s is the expected total discounted future reward from state s, following the policy.

6
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:22.833
Q of s and a is the same, but you commit to action a first.

7
00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:25.500
Here is why this matters.

8
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.987
The agent doesn't simulate the future.

9
00:00:27.987 --> 00:00:31.267
Its worth is already baked into the number on each state.

10
00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:34.800
The math engine is the Bellman equation.

11
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.967
A state's value is the immediate reward you get.

12
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:39.733
Plus gamma, the discount.

13
00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:42.405
Times the value of the state you land in.

14
00:00:42.405 --> 00:00:43.967
It's recursive bookkeeping.

15
00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:48.000
Let's compute it by hand, always walking east.

16
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.900
Stepping into the goal pays plus one, so that cell is worth one.

17
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:58.767
One step further back, the reward is one step away: zero point nine times one is zero point nine.

18
00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.662
Two steps away: zero point eight one.

19
00:01:01.662 --> 00:01:03.767
Value fades by gamma per step.

20
00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:06.367
The same thing in Python.

21
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:10.067
The terminal cell has no future, so its value is zero.

22
00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.233
The cell before it pays plus one.

23
00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:15.712
Each cell further back is gamma times its neighbor.

24
00:01:15.712 --> 00:01:18.767
Simulating episodes converges to the same number.

25
00:01:19.967 --> 00:01:22.767
Consider an agent scheduling satellite downlinks.

26
00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:26.500
It is only rewarded when data lands at the ground station.

27
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.300
A nearly full buffer with a pass in two minutes beats an empty buffer with no pass for an hour.

28
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.163
Neither pays anything now.

29
00:01:34.163 --> 00:01:35.667
Only their values differ.

30
00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:37.767
Let's recap.

31
00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:41.067
V of s is expected discounted future reward.

32
00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.867
Q of s and a commits to an action first.

33
00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:47.633
Bellman says: reward, plus gamma times the next value.

34
00:01:47.933 --> 00:01:50.410
Values make lookahead unnecessary.

35
00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.867
Next up: Q-learning.
